@startuml state_restart
!theme plain
title Restart State Machine (Improvement 3.3)

skinparam state {
    BackgroundColor<<idle>> #E8FDE8
    BackgroundColor<<active>> #FDE8E8
    BackgroundColor<<waiting>> #E8E8FD
    BackgroundColor<<done>> #FDF8E8
}

[*] --> IDLE

state IDLE <<idle>>
state NOTIFYING <<active>>
state AWAITING_ACK <<waiting>>
state RESTARTING <<active>>
state DONE <<done>>

IDLE --> NOTIFYING : detect_killed()\n[dead processes found]
NOTIFYING --> AWAITING_ACK : notifications_sent()
AWAITING_ACK --> RESTARTING : begin_restart()\n[all panels acknowledged]
AWAITING_ACK --> RESTARTING : check_timeout()\n[timeout exceeded]
RESTARTING --> DONE : restart_completed()
DONE --> IDLE : reset_to_idle()

IDLE : Normal operation
IDLE : Health check active

NOTIFYING : Dead process detected
NOTIFYING : Preparing notifications

AWAITING_ACK : Notifications sent
AWAITING_ACK : Waiting for all panels
AWAITING_ACK : to acknowledge

RESTARTING : All panels ready
RESTARTING : Restarting processes

DONE : Restart complete
DONE : Notifying panels

note right of AWAITING_ACK
  **Timeout Handling:**
  If panels don't acknowledge
  within timeout period,
  restart proceeds anyway
end note

note bottom of IDLE
  **RestartContext tracks:**
  - killed_processes
  - notified_panels
  - pending_panels
  - started_at timestamp
  - retry_count
end note

@enduml
